body:
Plan: `.pi/plans/2026-09-20-scripted-session/plan.md`

Modify: `tests/two_stage.rs`

Extend the existing fixture runner minimally so tests can invoke the binary with top-level opening arguments while retaining the fake fzf, fake tmux, dedicated `GROVE_TMUX_SOCKET`, Git environment isolation, and mutation support. Do not create a second fixture or contact the normal tmux server.

Reference: `tests/two_stage.rs:11-112` — temporary normal/bare/linked repository setup and fake subprocesses. Reference: `tests/two_stage.rs:120-197` — opening-flow runner and picker-count assertions. Reference: `tests/two_stage.rs:199-272` — argument-capable session runner pattern.

Add focused end-to-end cases proving:
- normal checkout plus configured preset creates/navigates without any picker;
- linked worktree plus configured preset uses linked naming/metadata;
- omitted preset opens only the layout picker and cancellation is a no-op;
- an explicit checkout outside configured roots (including empty roots if easiest) succeeds;
- unknown preset errors without tmux creation;
- matching worktree metadata reuses the session before preset lookup/picker;
- occupied preferred name retains existing suffix behavior;
- bare and non-Git explicit paths fail without picker/tmux mutation;
- picker-time checkout replacement remains blocked by second validation.

Use argv arguments throughout and assertions that preserve spaces/Unicode where the fixture already supports them. Avoid retesting Clap-only relative-path and dependency rules already covered in `src/main.rs`.

Acceptance: ISC-1 through ISC-7 and ISC-10 through ISC-12 have end-to-end evidence; ISC-A-1 and ISC-A-2 remain true; `cargo test --test two_stage` passes.

Dependencies: TODO-0001, TODO-0002, TODO-0003.
